enginespace: third-party notices

enginespace vendors files from kernelspace, in vendor/kernelspace/. This file carries
the notices that come with them, in two sections: kernelspace, and ts-fsrs, whose memory
model one of kernelspace's files transcribes. A third section, Fonts, carries the licences
of the faces the site self-hosts in public/fonts/. A fourth, vLLM, names the three files
that translate parts of vLLM to TypeScript, and a fifth, Quoted excerpts, covers the short
excerpts of nano-vllm, Mini-SGLang, vLLM and SGLang that the lessons, the claims and the
lifecycle model quote. The text of the Apache License 2.0, which several of these are
under, is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. The licence of enginespace's own code and content is
the owner's decision (O-3) and is not stated here: until it is decided, enginespace's own
code and content are all rights reserved.

============================================================================
kernelspace
============================================================================

The files that vendor/kernelspace/VENDOR.md lists, each with its SHA-256 and the terms it
is under, are copied, byte for byte, from kernelspace at commit
d478f91a0af590f03fcfd76ee73149fa70b28e51 (committed 2026-10-30). The other files under
vendor/kernelspace/ are enginespace's own: VENDOR.md, .gitattributes, and the type shims
shims/ambient.d.ts, shims/src/lib/learner/types.ts and shims/src/lib/ledger/types.ts, of
which the last two restate declarations from kernelspace's own types modules.

kernelspace's code, tests, fixtures and configuration are under the MIT License below. It
