============================================================================
vLLM
============================================================================

Parts of three files are translated to TypeScript from vLLM v0.33.0 and modified. Each
begins with a header that says so and points here. They keep the names of the Python
(snake_case turned into camelCase) and, where the logic is not trivial, the order of its
statements.

vLLM v0.33.0
  Source:    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, the tag v0.33.0, commit
             4ba787ec9959e566d3b587a796dff07673324da5
  Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
  Licence:   Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

packages/sim/steploop/graphs.ts, the model of CUDA graphs and their two dispatchers,
translates parts of these files of vLLM:
  vllm/v1/cudagraph_dispatcher.py        CudagraphDispatcher
  vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py  CudaGraphManager and BatchExecutionDescriptor
  vllm/v1/worker/gpu/lora_utils.py       get_lora_capture_cases
  vllm/lora/utils.py                     get_captured_lora_counts
  vllm/config/compilation.py             CUDAGraphMode,
                                         CompilationConfig.resolve_cudagraph_mode_and_sizes
                                         and adjust_cudagraph_sizes_for_spec_decode
  vllm/config/vllm.py                    VllmConfig._set_cudagraph_sizes
It also restates the fields of BatchDescriptor (vllm/forward_context.py) and the values of
AttentionCGSupport (vllm/v1/attention/backend.py).

tests/sim/graphs-oracle.ts, a second translation of the same two dispatchers that is
written to share no code with graphs.ts, translates parts of
vllm/v1/cudagraph_dispatcher.py, vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py,
vllm/v1/worker/gpu/lora_utils.py (get_lora_capture_cases) and vllm/lora/utils.py
(get_captured_lora_counts), and restates the values of CUDAGraphMode
(vllm/config/compilation.py).

tests/sim/kv-support.ts, whose vllmHit is the oracle of the hybrid KV model's search for a
prefix hit, translates parts of these files of vLLM:
  vllm/v1/core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py  find_longest_cache_hit of
                                                FullAttentionManager,
                                                SlidingWindowManager and MambaManager
  vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_coordinator.py          find_longest_cache_hit of
                                                HybridKVCacheCoordinator

vLLM's source files state their copyright as "Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"
and their licence as Apache-2.0, in a two-line header; the ten files named above read so at
the tag [measured 2026-11-08]. vLLM's LICENSE at the tag is the Apache License 2.0 with its
appendix unfilled (SHA-256
c71d239df91726fc519c6eb72d318ec65820627232b2f796219e87dcf35d0ab4), and vLLM has no NOTICE
file at the tag [measured 2026-11-08], so section 4(d) of the licence has no attribution
lines of vLLM's to carry.

LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt is the Apache License 2.0 as published at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt, fetched on 2026-11-08 (SHA-256
cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30). It is the text of
vLLM's LICENSE, apart from one blank line at the start. The Mooncake bullet above and the
section below point at it too.

